# ARK Two Implementations Rule

**Parent:** [communications-voice-cleanup-sprint-v1.md](../../docs/communications/communications-voice-cleanup-sprint-v1.md) · [ark-dependency-policy.mdc](ark-dependency-policy.mdc)

## Rule

**No abstraction survives without at least two production implementations.**

If there is exactly one runtime, one provider, or one transport in production today, do not introduce (or keep):

- Manager
- Strategy
- Provider selector
- Factory
- Adapter layer
- Interface whose only implementer is the one class you already have

**Do not replace one abstraction with a prettier abstraction.** Example of what to reject:

```text
TwilioVoiceTransport → VoiceTransportInterface → ArkVoiceTransport
```

When only `ArkVoiceTransport` ships, **`ArkVoiceTransport` is enough.**

## Litmus

Before adding or preserving a seam, ask:

> **Name the second production implementation that uses this abstraction today.**

If you cannot name it → **delete, inline, or rename** — do not generalize.

## Labels (audit pass — B1 classification)

Every inventory row gets **Classification** (what it is) and **Action** (what B2 may do). Plus **Proof** (evidence column).

| Classification | Meaning | Allowed action |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Dead** | Proven unused | Delete |
| **Legacy** | Referenced; scheduled for retirement | Keep (document why) |
| **Infrastructure** | Production runtime | Keep |
| **Future** | Planned phase (CallKit, …) | Keep |
| **Rename** | Good impl, wrong vocabulary | Rename only |
| **Unknown** | Cannot prove role | **Stop** — not Delete |

**Delete gate:** Who calls this? · What behavior depends on it? · What replaces it?  
All three answered with proof → Dead/Delete. Else → Unknown.

No "maybe." No naming-based deletion.

## Scope

Broader than telephony. Applies to transports, payment gateways, push providers, report engines, and any "we might support X someday" seam.

**Exception:** Test doubles and fakes in `tests/` do not count as a second production implementation.

## Voice cleanup (Phase B — ark-mobile)

**B1 before B2.** Inventory first; erasure second. See sprint doc.

**30-second test:** Clone ark-mobile → voice runtime is immediately `ArkVoiceTransport` → `sip_ua` → Asterisk. Not `VoiceProvider`, `TransportStrategy`, or `AsteriskVoiceTransport`.

**Naming:** Keep **`ArkVoiceTransport`** — ARK owns the client; Asterisk is execution, not the product name on the transport class.

Backend `TelephonyProviderManager` / Twilio-vs-Asterisk shims stay until VVX is boring, ARK Phone stops destabilizing production, and rollback is explicitly closed (Phase D).
